{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thank you for joining today's pre-approval huddle. As you know, the district's middle-school mathematics assessment is scheduled for May 14, 2027, and I've asked each of you to review the draft administration plan before I give it final approval. The plan currently calls for digital testing on school tablets, all 26 students testing together in Room 201, one proctor, graphing calculators available throughout the assessment, and completed materials stored in the general records cabinet. I'd like to go through each component systematically. Could each of you share your review findings, starting with any concerns you've identified?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Dr. Morris, I need to flag a concern with the room arrangement in the draft plan. My finalized roster does have 26 students, but the state administration manual limits a testing room to 14 students. I've already prepared Room 201 for 14 students and Room 202 for the remaining 12 students to comply with that requirement. However, I should note that this updated room plan has not yet been entered into the district tracker, so the draft plan still reflects all 26 students together in Room 201."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Dr. Morris, I need to flag a critical concern with the digital testing component of the draft plan. My device test found that the 26 assigned tablets cannot run the required secure testing application, and the district cannot obtain compatible devices before May 14. I contacted the assessment vendor, and they confirmed that paper booklets are authorized as an alternative. However, this result has not yet been added to the plan, so the draft still calls for digital testing on school tablets."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "Dr. Morris, I need to flag a concern with the storage component of the draft plan. My security review of the state testing agreement, which I completed this week, requires that completed assessment materials be sealed in tamper-evident envelopes and stored in a locked cabinet for exactly 30 calendar days. The draft plan currently calls for completed materials to be stored in the general records cabinet, which does not meet these requirements. I have not yet updated the storage field in the draft plan to reflect the necessary changes."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you all for your thorough reviews. Each of you has identified a critical compliance issue with the draft plan, and I appreciate you flagging these before I give final approval. Let me summarize what I'm hearing: Mr. Bell, the room capacity must be split into Room 201 for 14 students and Room 202 for 12 students per state manual limits. Ms. Shah, calculators must be four-function only and limited to section 2 of the assessment. Mr. Nguyen, the tablets can't run the secure testing application, so we need to switch to paper booklets as authorized by the vendor. Ms. Delgado, completed materials must be sealed in tamper-evident envelopes and stored in a locked cabinet for exactly 30 calendar days. Before I settle on the revised plan, I want to address one more component — the draft currently calls for one proctor. Given that we're now splitting students across two rooms, does anyone have concerns about whether one proctor is sufficient, or are there state requirements regarding proctor-to-student ratios or proctors per testing room that I should be aware of?"}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "I agree with Mr. Bell's recommendation. I don't have specific information about state requirements regarding proctor-to-student ratios or proctors per testing room beyond what I've already shared about calculator requirements. However, from a practical standpoint, having one proctor cover two rooms simultaneously would be very difficult to manage, especially during a state assessment where proper supervision and security are critical. I'd strongly recommend we confirm the state manual's requirements on this point before finalizing the plan."}
```

```json
